WEBVTT

00:02.250 --> 00:09.210
Episode 20: Nonstandard

00:02.250 --> 00:09.210
Episode 20: Nonstandard

00:11.580 --> 00:13.410
In third grade,

00:13.410 --> 00:16.620
I beat up a cocky high schooler.

00:14.720 --> 00:17.220
Handwriting

00:14.720 --> 00:17.220
Fun to Learn
Arithmetic

00:14.720 --> 00:17.220
Japanese

00:20.900 --> 00:24.620
Even if he was older, cocky is still cocky.

00:25.120 --> 00:27.730
He mocked me.

00:30.680 --> 00:33.710
And when I feel mocked,

00:33.710 --> 00:36.990
that's when the gong rings on the fight.

00:37.810 --> 00:39.680
It wasn't that fun.

00:39.680 --> 00:43.340
Trouncing a boring guy 
was naturally boring, too.

00:44.960 --> 00:46.980
Nice fight, boy!

00:50.500 --> 00:54.550
What kind of woman is your type?

00:55.670 --> 00:57.480
Who are you?

00:59.170 --> 01:01.570
My boredom was about 
to be flipped upside-down.

01:01.570 --> 01:03.560
That was the feeling she gave me.

02:26.060 --> 02:29.810
JUJUTSU KAISEN

02:47.120 --> 02:49.850
It's time to unleash my technique!

02:49.850 --> 02:52.370
Huh? Didn't you use it before?

02:52.370 --> 02:56.610
However! I have no time 
to explain my technique!

02:56.970 --> 02:59.700
So there's only one thing I can say to you.

03:00.260 --> 03:01.430
Don't stop!

03:01.770 --> 03:03.490
Believe in me!

03:03.920 --> 03:05.690
Okay! That's two, though!

03:07.940 --> 03:10.770
Let's analyze our opponent's cards.

03:11.150 --> 03:13.230
One is roots that emerge from the ground.

03:13.750 --> 03:19.130
That one probably gains power and speed 
the more it limits quantity and range.

03:19.420 --> 03:21.030
Then there's Wooden Ball.

03:21.030 --> 03:24.050
Each ball can attack once or twice, 
and then it's expended.

03:24.050 --> 03:29.040
They can remain airborne, 
and I have to watch for delayed activation.

03:29.040 --> 03:30.520
Then there's Cursed Bud.

03:30.520 --> 03:33.520
That's probably what Fushiguro got hit with.

03:33.520 --> 03:35.440
Guess you're out if even if one of those hits.

03:35.440 --> 03:38.300
Though I want to believe that 
means it can't fire too many.

03:38.710 --> 03:39.940
Then there's Flower Field.

03:39.940 --> 03:42.130
It looks like that relaxes you,

03:42.130 --> 03:44.490
but its earlier wounds are throwing it off.

03:44.490 --> 03:46.280
No need to be too wary of it.

03:46.280 --> 03:49.780
Then there's that unleashed left arm...

03:51.620 --> 03:55.290
And the possibility that 
all of those are bluffs!

03:55.800 --> 04:00.110
However, it doesn't matter what a 
technique is if you don't let them activate it!

04:00.850 --> 04:06.550
Even accounting for unexpected situations,

04:05.580 --> 04:06.550
*Self-Proclaimed IQ 530,000

04:08.580 --> 04:13.040
my IQ 530,000 mental CPU 
produces only one conclusion:

04:15.310 --> 04:16.960
Victory!

04:18.900 --> 04:22.400
Because I'm not alone,

04:23.150 --> 04:24.030
Brother!

04:25.100 --> 04:26.950
Because you're here!

04:36.330 --> 04:37.380
Toudou!

04:43.920 --> 04:44.950
Toudou!

04:47.370 --> 04:49.350
That's one down.

05:01.700 --> 05:02.820
Oh, Toudou!

05:03.090 --> 05:04.480
I see.

05:04.480 --> 05:06.000
It's simple...

05:07.440 --> 05:10.240
and therefore a troublesome technique.

05:10.240 --> 05:11.160
Yeah.

05:11.160 --> 05:15.200
My technique swaps my position 
with my opponent's.

05:15.200 --> 05:16.750
Boogie Woogie!

05:18.770 --> 05:19.460
Toudou!

05:19.460 --> 05:23.070
Shh! We'll end this before 
it can get used to it.

05:26.700 --> 05:28.420
By the way,

05:28.420 --> 05:29.940
clapping my hands

05:29.940 --> 05:31.600
is necessary to activate it!

05:46.140 --> 05:48.070
Their builds are too different!

05:48.070 --> 05:50.240
There's a big difference after they swap!

05:53.810 --> 05:55.760
Is he swapping with me?

05:55.760 --> 05:58.440
Or is he swapping with Sukuna's vessel?

05:58.440 --> 06:02.880
Every time he claps, that split 
decision makes my thoughts falter!

06:08.160 --> 06:10.470
Oh, no! I can't...

06:28.320 --> 06:30.240
...break out of this!

06:36.920 --> 06:38.290
They're using that again!

06:41.560 --> 06:44.770
Using Black Flash consecutively 
isn't anything amazing.

06:48.030 --> 06:54.030
\hNanami Kento, record holder for consecutive Black Flash uses, speaks\h

06:48.440 --> 06:54.530
Though it is difficult to produce more than 
twice in a row, or on a different day.

06:54.530 --> 06:58.710
It doesn't matter if you land 
the first by fluke or skill.

06:58.710 --> 07:00.350
Once they land a Black Flash,

07:00.350 --> 07:05.170
sorcerers temporarily enter 
a state athletes call "the zone."

07:05.800 --> 07:09.050
The manipulation of cursed energy 
that they normally control consciously

07:09.050 --> 07:11.320
becomes as natural as breathing.

07:11.320 --> 07:16.560
There's a sense of omnipotence, 
like everything else revolves around them...

07:16.560 --> 07:19.060
That might be a good way to put it.

07:20.180 --> 07:22.540
My record?

07:25.650 --> 07:26.960
Four times.

07:27.570 --> 07:29.670
I just got lucky.

07:36.400 --> 07:37.740
Black Flash!

07:38.180 --> 07:39.540
Brother,

07:39.540 --> 07:42.210
I always get that premonition from you!

07:50.160 --> 07:51.860
Black Flash!

07:56.500 --> 07:57.600
Black Flash!

07:58.050 --> 08:00.100
Three in a row!

08:00.500 --> 08:02.230
Don't get cocky!

08:04.930 --> 08:06.040
Swapping positions?!

08:06.040 --> 08:07.790
What I have to be wary of right now

08:08.630 --> 08:10.000
is Sukuna's...

08:11.960 --> 08:13.490
They didn't swap?!

08:17.660 --> 08:19.260
Clapping my hands

08:19.260 --> 08:22.080
doesn't necessarily mean 
I'm activating my technique!

08:22.080 --> 08:25.500
It's simple, but easy to fall for!

08:26.470 --> 08:32.180
I'm getting that same premonition of 
my boredom being turned upside-down!

08:36.980 --> 08:38.560
Black Flash!

08:41.160 --> 08:43.980
JUJUTSU KAISEN

08:46.630 --> 08:48.960
JUJUTSU KAISEN

09:31.670 --> 09:33.600
It's attacking before each swap!

09:33.600 --> 09:36.910
It's getting used to Toudou's technique!

09:37.410 --> 09:41.230
But that Black Flash rush hurt it.

09:41.230 --> 09:42.850
We can exorcise it!

09:42.850 --> 09:44.180
Together!

09:45.140 --> 09:49.220
This is the first time 
I've ever been hurt so badly,

09:49.850 --> 09:51.880
and despite that...

09:54.180 --> 09:57.700
my delight in this battle isn't waning!

10:15.860 --> 10:18.220
His technique reveal was full of lies!

10:18.860 --> 10:22.600
He's able to swap two others, as well?!

10:22.860 --> 10:23.980
Toudou!

10:24.830 --> 10:26.840
He's protecting me!

10:27.100 --> 10:29.560
Don't worry, Brother!

10:30.320 --> 10:34.110
By seriously hardening my 
body and cursed energy,

10:34.570 --> 10:39.070
I'll easily repel these buds!

10:45.260 --> 10:46.970
Are you sure?

10:49.870 --> 10:52.330
T-Takada-chan?!

10:53.940 --> 10:57.790
You remember Fushiguro-kun's injuries?

10:57.790 --> 10:59.590
Of course I remember!

10:59.590 --> 11:02.810
Those are the cursed buds about 
to slam into me right now!

11:02.810 --> 11:03.930
That's why I'mâ€”

11:03.930 --> 11:05.450
But remember,

11:05.450 --> 11:09.170
Fushiguro-kun's buds had grown a little.

11:12.940 --> 11:16.320
You think they grew by absorbing his blood?

11:16.320 --> 11:18.300
That's not impossible.

11:18.300 --> 11:20.950
But you're facing a cursed spirit.

11:21.410 --> 11:24.150
What's most likely?

11:28.960 --> 11:30.400
Cursed energy!

11:30.400 --> 11:31.900
Happened in 0.01 seconds

11:39.130 --> 11:41.150
He dispelled his cursed 
energy right before impact?

11:41.150 --> 11:42.450
He figured it out?!

11:43.040 --> 11:45.770
The harder they defend with cursed energy,

11:45.770 --> 11:48.170
the stronger those buds become!

11:49.150 --> 11:51.350
Her next one's the national?

11:51.350 --> 11:53.350
*National Handshake Event

11:53.350 --> 11:55.860
I'll have to thank her then,

11:56.350 --> 11:57.520
won't I?

12:06.930 --> 12:08.980
Hey, special-grade cursed spirit,

12:09.960 --> 12:14.320
I know you've realized 
I didn't tell you everything then.

12:14.900 --> 12:19.210
But there's one more thing 
you should be thinking about:

12:19.550 --> 12:22.620
what counts as a target for Boogie Woogie!

12:23.870 --> 12:27.150
With what can I swap within 
the range of my technique?

12:27.150 --> 12:28.870
Only creatures?

12:28.870 --> 12:30.170
Non!

12:30.170 --> 12:34.380
My technique works on cursed corpses 
and inanimate objects, too.

12:34.380 --> 12:36.400
So the answer is...

12:36.970 --> 12:39.960
Anything possessing cursed 
energy above a certain level!

12:43.060 --> 12:45.940
Hey, special-grade cursed spirit, 
have you noticed?

12:46.620 --> 12:50.490
We're back at that spot again.

12:50.790 --> 12:53.400
This is where it lies waiting.

12:59.360 --> 13:02.550
Maki-san's special-grade 
cursed tool is in the riverbed.

13:03.450 --> 13:06.040
The trees on its are face 
are especially fragile.

13:09.390 --> 13:10.640
The river?!

13:11.320 --> 13:14.140
What did I swap places with?

13:16.090 --> 13:17.970
Special-grade cursed tool,

13:24.840 --> 13:26.280
Playful Cloud!

13:34.480 --> 13:37.900
Even a blow from a special-grade cursed 
tool imbued with my cursed energy

13:37.900 --> 13:39.920
didn't completely take it down?

13:52.960 --> 13:56.300
Plants don't generate cursed energy.

13:56.800 --> 14:03.700
So my left arm steals the life from plants 
and converts it to cursed energy.

14:05.330 --> 14:08.490
But that never gets returned to me.

14:08.490 --> 14:11.600
It all goes to this flower offering.

14:11.600 --> 14:14.660
I didn't want to use this if I didn't have to.

14:23.090 --> 14:24.190
Toudou!

14:24.190 --> 14:25.480
Stay away, Brother!

14:25.480 --> 14:27.830
Its cursed energy output is incredible!

14:27.830 --> 14:33.070
But it will be easy for you 
to avoid with your technique.

14:33.070 --> 14:35.470
So what shall I do?

14:36.560 --> 14:38.030
Domain Exâ€”

14:40.960 --> 14:42.100
The veil!

15:09.530 --> 15:11.570
I see.

15:11.570 --> 15:15.100
I thought he sounded 
pretty good without the amp,

15:15.430 --> 15:18.390
but this old man is the amp himself.

15:18.390 --> 15:20.760
His technique amplifies the tune he plays

15:20.760 --> 15:23.630
and launches it as cursed energy.

15:24.240 --> 15:26.690
He's a predictable mid-range fighter.

15:26.690 --> 15:29.570
It's obvious he doesn't 
want me getting close.

15:32.070 --> 15:34.300
Let's make a wallet

15:34.300 --> 15:36.990
full of that old man smell!

15:43.000 --> 15:44.210
Roger that.

15:44.210 --> 15:46.720
Nishimiya, you keep going, too, 
and head to Shouko.

15:49.100 --> 15:50.330
It's okay.

15:50.330 --> 15:52.010
Mei-san has eyes on Miwa.

15:55.160 --> 15:57.490
Thank God it didn't cut off my reception.

15:57.490 --> 16:00.270
Guess that's only natural, 
given the effect of the veil.

16:00.770 --> 16:05.400
There's someone working with either 
a curse user or curses at Jujutsu Tech.

16:06.620 --> 16:08.890
Looks like he wasn't mistaken.

16:10.850 --> 16:11.740
Huh?

16:15.240 --> 16:18.060
I thought I cut you for sure.

16:18.990 --> 16:20.260
A human?

16:20.920 --> 16:22.020
A curse user?!

16:24.180 --> 16:26.180
This is my problem...

16:29.350 --> 16:31.730
This is nice, isn't it?

16:33.020 --> 16:35.350
Juuzou made it for me.

16:36.330 --> 16:38.220
Didn't you run into him earlier?

16:39.300 --> 16:43.730
You're weak, so have the 
sword hold your hand, too.

16:44.110 --> 16:44.970
...he said.

16:47.980 --> 16:51.580
Hey, what will you give me, lady?

16:52.110 --> 16:54.990
Girls hate you, don't they?

16:55.330 --> 16:58.480
You meet someone new, 
and all you talk about is yourself.

16:59.140 --> 17:00.540
I'll charge you for this.

17:00.540 --> 17:04.390
What makes you think you're a good 
enough listener to charge for it?

17:05.250 --> 17:06.720
You guys!

17:05.250 --> 17:08.300
Shut up! Stop picking fights 
in moments like these!

17:09.810 --> 17:13.500
Wow! So many girls!

17:13.500 --> 17:14.880
I'm so popular!

17:16.060 --> 17:18.430
Were you listening to me?

17:18.430 --> 17:20.140
I'll cover you.

17:20.470 --> 17:22.600
Be careful not to get hit in the crossfire.

17:22.600 --> 17:24.840
You be careful not to hit me!

17:31.980 --> 17:33.600
The veil lifted?!

17:34.340 --> 17:35.730
For real?

17:35.730 --> 17:38.130
It hasn't even been 30 minutes, has it?

17:38.480 --> 17:39.770
Time to run!

17:41.490 --> 17:44.330
What was his deal?

17:46.990 --> 17:50.030
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

17:51.990 --> 17:55.590
I can see that slick coat rack now!

17:58.290 --> 17:59.830
So...

17:59.830 --> 18:01.830
Where should I start?

18:05.310 --> 18:06.390
Huh?

18:11.540 --> 18:14.360
Looks like this is as far as we go.

18:14.980 --> 18:17.350
Huh? Gojou-sensei?!

18:26.150 --> 18:30.630
Yuuji's on a much higher level than before.

18:31.750 --> 18:33.960
I see! Aoi!

18:34.400 --> 18:36.960
Of course he'd be a great match for Yuuji.

18:37.470 --> 18:39.880
Looks like they're 
fighting the special-grade,

18:39.880 --> 18:41.640
but I shouldn't have to 
worry about them now.

18:42.550 --> 18:44.950
Which means my priority should be...

18:47.510 --> 18:49.020
You.

18:49.470 --> 18:51.740
Rack! Rack! Rack!

18:52.300 --> 18:53.550
Don't kill him!

19:03.920 --> 19:06.540
We have a lot to ask this guy.

19:07.440 --> 19:09.470
Don't let him die on us.

19:09.470 --> 19:11.030
Go on, treat him.

19:16.380 --> 19:19.610
The guy near Utahime disappeared.

19:20.480 --> 19:23.040
Guess he found a means to escape.

19:24.150 --> 19:25.930
That just leaves that one?

19:26.320 --> 19:28.210
One adept at running, too.

19:29.330 --> 19:31.780
It's some distance from Yuuji.

19:32.450 --> 19:33.700
Oh, well.

19:34.310 --> 19:36.870
Guess I'll be a little rough.

19:37.570 --> 19:39.890
Cursed Technique Amplification: Blue.

19:40.380 --> 19:42.810
Cursed Technique Reversal: Red.

19:46.690 --> 19:48.220
I'm withdrawing.

19:48.220 --> 19:51.710
I'm not arrogant enough 
to face Gojou Satoru.

19:51.710 --> 19:52.990
Screw you!

19:52.990 --> 19:55.530
What were you all trying to do here?!

19:56.460 --> 19:58.090
Wait, Brother!

19:58.090 --> 20:00.030
Why are you stopping me, Toudou?!

20:01.890 --> 20:03.960
Don't take another step forward...

20:07.610 --> 20:09.210
or you'll get caught in it.

20:13.010 --> 20:14.220
Hollow...

20:17.420 --> 20:18.630
Purple!

20:45.650 --> 20:48.170
He's just as nonstandard as ever.

20:50.100 --> 20:53.410
Now we can't tell if it was exorcised or not.

20:54.960 --> 20:57.880
Ow! It hurts!

20:57.880 --> 20:58.860
Quiet!

20:59.110 --> 21:00.950
Yay!

21:00.950 --> 21:02.720
That settles everything!

21:04.280 --> 21:06.910
Or I guess it doesn't.

21:16.130 --> 21:17.930
I wonder if Hanami's safe.

21:19.170 --> 21:21.550
That's mission complete.

22:54.930 --> 22:57.430
Juju Stroll

22:56.770 --> 22:57.430
Salmon.

22:57.430 --> 22:59.060
Q: Dog or cat?

22:59.060 --> 23:06.900
Q: Are you a dog person or a cat person?

22:59.520 --> 23:00.600
Dog?

23:01.180 --> 23:03.710
No, maybe cat?

23:04.030 --> 23:06.900
Wait, maybe dog if it's a big dog!

23:06.900 --> 23:08.650
Q: Are you a dog person or a cat person?

23:07.750 --> 23:08.640
Dog.

23:08.650 --> 23:10.570
Dog, I think?

23:08.650 --> 23:12.700
Q: Are you a dog person or a cat person?

23:10.570 --> 23:12.700
What? I definitely prefer cats.

23:12.700 --> 23:14.240
Q: Are you a dog person or a cat person?

23:13.190 --> 23:14.240
Salmon.

23:14.240 --> 23:19.040
Q: Are you a dog person or a cat person?

23:14.640 --> 23:16.480
The answer's obviously pandas!

23:16.480 --> 23:19.040
You want me to kill you?! Huh?!

23:19.920 --> 23:23.850
Everyone hates me,

23:23.850 --> 23:26.000
don't they?

23:26.000 --> 23:28.220
Well, there were only two choices.

23:28.220 --> 23:29.920
Just leave him be.

23:36.470 --> 23:39.930
Episode 21:
Jujutsu Koshien
